# packaging/required-entries.list — the shared required-set constant
# (T3, 0.13). One list, four consumers: cut-release.sh gate 4,
# install.sh's post-stage verification, the doctor installed-set
# check, and the tests that pin this file. Do NOT hand-maintain the
# list anywhere else — every consumer parses this file (the two
# inline eight-entry lists in cut-release.sh and install.sh were the
# drift risk).
#
# Sections (a bare word on its own line switches the section):
#   REQUIRED — runtime entries that must exist in the package AND in
#              every install (filesystem check by install.sh and
#              doctor).
#   STATE    — paths that must never be SHIPPED in a package manifest
#              (gate 4's state-free rule: any path ELEMENT matching a
#              STATE entry is an offender). The install root may
#              legitimately hold venv/ (install.sh creates it);
#              doctor's install-filesystem sub-rule therefore checks
#              STATE minus venv.
#
# Format: one entry per line, relative to the package/install root.
# "#" starts a comment; blank lines are ignored. Parsed by the
# required_entries() helper below (bash) and by doctor.py (python) —
# both must agree; tests pin the file against both consumers.

REQUIRED
bin/hive
lib/core/agent-spawn.sh
lib/core/agent-harness.py
lib/hive_mcp/server.py
lib/dashboard/server.js
etc/config.defaults.toml
etc/config.template.toml
packaging/requirements.txt
# The constant pins itself: it ships (entries.list) and every
# consumer requires it at the install root — a drift that
# drops it fails gate 4, post-stage, and doctor at once.
packaging/required-entries.list
# T1 (0.14): the venv lock — the install's Python environment is a
# reproducible artifact (install.sh installs from it; doctor's
# "venv lock" check cross-checks the venv against it).
packaging/requirements.lock.txt

STATE
.company
.worktrees
venv
dist
__pycache__
.git
